INT. THRONE ROOM OF OSRIC - DAY

A hall of cracked marble and tattered banners. Dust in the shafts of light.

KING OSRIC, 60s, slumped on a tarnished throne, tugs his gray beard. LADY VANETH, 40s, in a mourning gown, stands rigid at the foot of the dais. PIBBLE, the court fool, 30s, juggles three wooden spoons on the steps.

KING OSRIC
Vaneth. Another harvest report?

LADY VANETH
The fields lie fallow, Majesty.

PIBBLE
(together with Lady Vaneth)
The fields lie fallow, Majesty.

^LADY VANETH
The fields lie fallow, Majesty.

Both stop. Pibble catches a spoon and bows. Lady Vaneth does not.

KING OSRIC
You rehearse together, I see.

PIBBLE
We have a duet, sire.

LADY VANETH
We have no such thing.

KING OSRIC
Pibble, play me a song.

Pibble tucks the spoons under his arm and hums. The King nods slowly.
